#. type: Content of: <messages><msg>
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:1 docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:5 messages/po4a/en.xml:678
#, no-wrap
msgid "Habitat RPC"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Habitat RPC** is the **single business channel** between Habitat clients and the agent runtime. The TypeScript constant is `HABITAT_RPC_VERSION`. Transport:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:11
msgid ""
"**WebSocket** — long-lived connection at **`/rpc/v1`** (connect handshake + "
"heartbeat; Habitat RPC `req`/`res`/`evt` envelope)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:11
msgid ""
"**HTTP REST** — stateless GET/POST at **`/rpc/v1/{method/path}`** (plain "
"JSON body or query; `Authorization: Bearer`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:13
msgid ""
"Implemented in [`src/shared/habitat-rpc/`](../../src/shared/habitat-rpc/) "
"(WS envelope + HTTP REST helpers) and [`src/host/platform/habitat/http-rest-"
"router.ts`](../../src/host/platform/habitat/http-rest-router.ts) (HTTP "
"adapter). Feature method schemas live under [`src/shared/rpc-contract/`]"
"(../../src/shared/rpc-contract/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:15
msgid ""
"Binary HTTP methods (e.g. `tts.synthesize`, companion assets, TLS PEM/QR) "
"use Habitat RPC REST with registry `request` / `response` encoding. Public "
"probes (`health.probe`, `tls.ca.*`) are Habitat RPC methods with `auth: "
"optional`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tools: MCP first, remote registration rare"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Situation                                                    | Mechanism                                                             |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Peer is dialable (has a stable inbound MCP/HTTP listener)    | **MCP** — expose tools to each other                                  |\n"
"| Product UI (Chat, Task, Settings, …)                         | Habitat RPC only — **no** remote-tool attach                          |\n"
"| Unreachable local app (no inbound listener Habitat can dial) | App **actively connects** and registers remote tools over Habitat RPC |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:25
msgid ""
"Desktop companion is the in-tree example of the third row. Future "
"independent local apps may do the same without being a Portal shell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remote tool registration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:29
msgid "After Habitat RPC `connect`, an unreachable local app calls:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:33
msgid ""
"`remote_tools.attach` — registers with `app_id` + optional `instance_id` "
"(omit on first register; Habitat assigns; same machine may have multiple "
"instances)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:33
msgid "`tool.register` — publishes local tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:33
msgid ""
"Habitat later sends `tool.call` events; the app replies with `tool.result` / "
"`tool.error`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:35
msgid ""
"Routing key is **`instance_id`** (follows the connecting application, not "
"the Portal shell). Tool names use the `remote_{app}_{instance}_{local}` form "
"(legacy `remote_*` / `sap:*` still parsed for stored sessions)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Call routing:** On `tool.register`, Habitat binds each tool handler to that Outpost connection (`instance_id`). Invoking a registered tool sends `tool.call` on that bound channel — no session `outpost_*` check and no re-parse of the tool name for routing. Disconnect unregisters the toolset. Session `outpost_app_id` / `outpost_instance_id` remains optional metadata (e.g. which outpost opened the chat). `workspace_root` may still be taken from conversation meta for the payload only.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:39
msgid ""
"Server: [`src/host/capabilities/outpost/`](../../src/host/capabilities/"
"outpost/). Client helper: `createRemoteToolsHabitatAttach` in `@freeanima/"
"shared/rpc-contract`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoints"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ws://{habitat_host}:{port}/rpc/v1\n"
"http://{habitat_host}:{port}/rpc/v1/task/list\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:48
msgid ""
"Helpers: `resolveHabitatRpcWsUrl`, `buildHabitatRestRequest` in `@freeanima/"
"shared/habitat-rpc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "Client profiles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:55
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Profile          | Attach                          | Typical consumer                                                |\n"
"| ---------------- | ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Bundled SPA      | **No**                          | Chat, task, notification, diary, email                          |\n"
"| Remote-tool host | **Yes** (`remote_tools.attach`) | companion (overlay WebView-host); future independent local apps |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:57
msgid ""
"Bundled SPA shares **one** Habitat RPC WebSocket per page load. Product "
"modules pass a simple `platform` channel (e.g. `\"chat\"`), never a remote-"
"tool `instance_id`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <messages><msg>
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:58 messages/po4a/en.xml:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconnect"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:61
msgid ""
"Use `runHabitatRpcTransport` for connect, heartbeat, and exponential "
"backoff. On detach or socket close, Habitat unregisters tools for that "
"`instance_id`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ops/habitat-rpc.md:62
msgid ""
"See also: [`companion.md`](../modules/companion.md), [`architecture.md`](../"
"product/architecture.md)."
msgstr ""
